      "outputs": [],
      "title": "The LOOK wire",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "The **look** output carries the accumulated grade stack.\n\nIt is optional \u2014 images flow without it \u2014 but wiring it through means\n**PW Look I/O** can save the whole chain as a `.look`, or bake the\ncolour part to a `.cube`, and tell you exactly which parts a LUT\ncould not carry."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1020,
        1420
      ],
      "size": [
        660,
        260
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 3,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Analysis",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "**PW Palette** pulls the colours out of the graded frame.\nIts `palette` output can feed **PW Look**'s gradient map, so the ramp\nis built from the image's own colours.\n\n**PW Scopes** passes the image through untouched and renders a\nhistogram, waveform and RGB parade beside it."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        40,
        460
      ],
      "size": [
        340,
        240
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 4,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Starts neutral",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Every control starts at pass-through, so dropping this in changes\nnothing until you move something.\n\nTry a preset on **PW Look** first \u2014 they render on *your* image."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
